  "observations": [
    "Red-brown brick body, cream/beige ornamental trim, grey granite plinth, painted red standing-seam roof.",
    "North end is symmetric: central three tall arched windows above low arched central window; two wooden doors flank centre, two shorter arched windows over each door; seven upper openings across main facade.",
    "Central raised gable has a single slender round-headed window, circular medallions, cream horizontal bands and stepped brick pilasters.",
    "Central tall openings roughly 0.8-1.0m wide and 3.0-3.4m tall; lower sills about 3m above ground. Photo perspective makes measurements uncertain by 20-30 percent.",
    "Two paired side upper openings roughly 0.8-1.0m wide and 1.5-1.9m tall.",
    "Left long wall shows small rectangular white-framed upper windows and continuous glazed clerestory below red roof; no full-height curtain glazing.",
    "Pavement is pale warm grey rectangular concrete slabs; street dark neutral asphalt with patch edges and a light granite kerb.",
    "Retained local close-up 103304670P_37_v0_f_l_179223953576.jpg confirms three tall central arched windows, each with two glazing columns and four horizontal pane divisions; lower central triplet and narrow upper gable window. Pale trim is warm grey-beige.",
    "June 2026 Look Around panorama 569620272610193160, 1.4 m from shot camera: north entrance datum N2000 5.10 m from shipped lidar terrain, 1.06 m above building minimum base. Elevation offsets preserve surveyed roof height and expose the door threshold.",
    "Current reference confirms muted red-brown brick, beige-grey trim, paired arched entrance lights, and a white concrete / dark ribbon-glass neighbour; the teal source sample was a metal doorway.",
    "June 2026 north-end perspective: central three clear openings are about 46 px wide and 142 px tall against an approximately 840 px facade width; retain a tall 3.2/1.05 aspect ratio after applying the street datum.",
    "June2026 north facade: outer masonry piers occupy about18% of the width each. Door centres and paired sidelights sit near28%/72%, not at the facade edges; central window centres about42%/50%/58%. Corner pediments reach about69% of the total height. Projecting copings, alternating pier courses and shoulder arches are modeled from measured profiles; depth estimated0.12\u20130.30m, uncertain\u00b10.10m."
  ],
